Subject: [PATCH 18/67] =?UTF-8?q?fix(aligram):=20D-05=20=E2=80=94=20scope?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20blob=20identity=20by=20account?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Verified: blob storage is per-account (AliGramFileCopy.getBlobDir) but
PreservedBlob had no account column and getByDocumentKey /
getByPhotoKey / getBlobsByDocument / getBlobsByPhoto filtered only on
(documentId|photoId, dcId, size, sha256), so the second account's ref
was bound to a blob file living only in the first account's dir
(noteCopiedFile found no file, startup split-brain marked the ref
UNAVAILABLE; purgeAccount(A) deleted the file under B's ref). Fix:
PreservedBlob.accountId (Room v2, MIGRATION_1_2 adds the column with
default 0) + account filter on all four identity lookups +
account-scoped blob id (new AliGramEligibility.blobIdFor(accountId,
...) overload — 'a<N>_' prefix for N != 0; account 0 keeps the legacy
id so migrated v1 rows stay valid; the 5-arg form is unchanged, its
format is pinned by tests). The v1 indices are deliberately unchanged
so the migration stays a single ALTER TABLE (Room validates indices
after a manual migration). findBlobForIdentity is account-scoped too,
so policy (ii) can no longer bind a revision to another account's
bytes. sweepRefcountZeroBlobs now deletes an orphaned blob's file from
every account directory (pre-D-05 / migrated rows may name a file in
another account's dir). The CI build will generate the new v2 schema
JSON under TMessagesProj/schemas/ (room.schemaLocation is configured).
